  "definition": "A leaderboard is a public, continuously updated ranking of systems or models against a shared benchmark dataset and fixed evaluation protocol, typically reporting standardised metrics on held-out test sets. Leaderboards make model comparison transparent and reproducible, drive competitive progress in machine learning and adjacent fields, and increasingly incorporate human preference voting \u2014 whilst also inviting over-fitting, benchmark gaming and metric myopia when rankings are treated as ends in themselves.",
